						<article class="project-template project-template--private">
							<div>
								<div class="project-meta" aria-label="Project status">
									<span class="project-meta__category">Full end-to-end OCR pipeline for desktop</span>
									<span class="project-meta__status">Active development</span>
									<span class="project-meta__release">No public release yet</span>
								</div>
								<h3>GlujLens</h3>
								<p>GlujLens is a cross-platform desktop pipeline for window, frame, and text detection, OCR, translation, and optional image processing. I’m designing compact neural networks for NPUs, GPUs, and AVX2 CPUs, targeting sub-200 ms inference on 1920 × 1080 images within a 1.5–2 TFLOP FP16 compute budget.</p>
								<p>ONNX Runtime and FP16/INT8 models provide hardware-portable inference. Local training uses Python, PyTorch, and AMD ROCm/HIP; the modular pipeline supports configurable OCR and translation providers, including Tesseract and purpose-trained models.</p>
							</div>
							<ul class="project-tags"> 
								<li>C#</li>
								<li>Python</li>  
								<li>.NET 10</li>
							    <li>Avalonia UI</li>
							    <li>FP16/INT8</li>
							    <li>PyTorch</li>
							    <li>ONNX Runtime</li>
							    <li>ROCm/HIP training</li>
								<li>Cross-platform</li>
							</ul>
							<div class="project-access-state">
								<span class="project-access-state__icon" aria-hidden="true">
									<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><rect x="5" y="10" width="14" height="10" rx="2"/><path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3M12 14v2"/></svg>
								</span>
								<span><strong>Proprietary project</strong><small>Source code, models, and development builds are private.</small></span>
							</div>
						</article>
						<article class="project-template project-template--public">
							<div>
								<div class="project-meta" aria-label="Project status">
									<span class="project-meta__category">Vendor-neutral hardware benchmark for Windows</span>
									<span class="project-meta__version">Version 0.4.0</span>
									<span class="project-meta__release project-meta__release--public">Public release</span>
								</div>
								<h3>Gluj-Bench</h3>
								<p>Gluj-Bench is a vendor-neutral Windows x64 benchmark built in Rust with a Slint interface and a separate worker using versioned JSON IPC for progress reporting and cancellation. It measures CPU cache and RAM bandwidth and latency, AVX2/FMA vector and matrix workloads, and Vulkan GPU vector, FP16/INT8 cooperative-matrix, memory bandwidth, and system-RAM offload performance.</p>
								<p>Configurable dataset sweeps, sample statistics, and interactive graphs show how throughput changes under memory pressure, with separate GPU execution and end-to-end timings. Persistent history and shareable PNG snapshots embed results for comparison imports. GitHub Actions automates checks, tests, and release builds.</p>
							</div>
							<ul class="project-tags">
								<li>Rust 2024</li><li>Slint</li><li>Vulkan</li><li>GLSL/SPIR-V</li><li>AVX2/FMA</li><li>Multithreading</li><li>JSON IPC</li><li>GitHub Actions</li><li>Windows x64</li><li>GPL-3.0-only</li>
							</ul>
							<div class="project-actions" aria-label="Gluj-Bench links">
								<a class="project-action project-action--source" href="https://github.com/githubdood21/Gluj-Bench" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
									<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 4H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v13a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h13a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-3M14 3h7v7M10 14 21 3"/></svg>
									<span>View source</span>
